      "significance": "notable",
      "hasDiff": true,
      "ai": {
        "model": "bai/qwen3.8-flash",
        "v": 5,
        "title": "SDK auto-retries interrupted streams via source-tagged error chunks",
        "summary": "The SDK now detects silent stream endings (connection cuts, reasoning output-limit hits) and yields source-tagged error chunks instead of ending the turn. The agent loop forces a retry step, capped at 3 consecutive recoveries, while the CLI UI shows a transient retrying status via `setIsRetrying`. Core changes span `sdk/src/impl/stream-interruption.ts` (detection), `common/src/types/contracts/llm.ts` (`StreamRecoverySource` type), and `cli/src/utils/sdk-event-handlers.ts` (UI state). `MAX_CONSECUTIVE_STREAM_RECOVERIES` limits retries; sourceless errors remain silent inline tool failures.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "at": "2026-09-14T15:39:06.593Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "When the assistant is in the middle of answering you and the connection drops, or it runs out of space while thinking and never gives an answer, the CLI used to just stop and your turn ended incomplete. It will now silently try again for you instead, showing a small 'retrying' note, and it will keep retrying up to three times before giving up. The change affects anyone using the command-line interface today and only triggers on these specific drop-and-die moments, not on ordinary tool errors.",
        "model": "vyce/deepseek-v4.1",
        "v": 4,
