      "significance": "notable",
      "hasDiff": true,
      "ai": {
        "model": "deepseek-v4.1",
        "v": 11,
        "title": "Hide context-pruner agent blocks in CLI UI",
        "summary": "The HIDDEN_AGENT_IDS constant now uses 'context-pruner' as a substring match instead of the publisher-qualified 'codebuff/context-pruner', so both bundled and fully-qualified agent ids like 'codebuff/context-pruner@1.0.0' are matched and excluded from rendering. The spawn_agents handler in sdk-event-handlers.ts skips hidden agents entirely during block creation and streaming-agent registration, preventing lingering empty blocks, while the new stripHiddenAgentBlocks helper in message-block-helpers.ts cleans persisted transcripts of context-pruner blocks that were saved before the live-stream filter was in place.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "audience": "end-users",
        "evidence": "In cli/src/utils/constants.ts, HIDDEN_AGENT_IDS changed from ['codebuff/context-pruner'] as const to ['context-pruner'] as const; in cli/src/utils/sdk-event-handlers.ts, handleSpawnAgentsToolCall now filters out hidden agents before creating blocks or spawn info; in cli/src/utils/message-block-helpers.ts, the new stripHiddenAgentBlocks function recursively removes hidden agent blocks while preserving array indices",
        "userVisible": true,
        "confidence": "high",
        "unknowns": "The diff does not show whether context-pruner was newly introduced or has been running in prior sessions, nor how existing persisted chats without the filter are migrated.",
